== U5 lever re-projection: fast kernel segments from ckpt350k (trie form) ==
(successor re-measurement, 2026-08-23; poll harness fixed to walk ONLY the
launched job's descendants — the first harness took max over all lean pids
and was polluted by a sibling lane's build, so the k2000 peak below is
reported as cap-bounded, not polled)

-- fastseg-k2000 (48G cap, timeout 3600) --
tag=fastseg-k2000-48G rc=137 wall_s=507 peak=cap-bounded (~48G cgroup; polluted poll read 51,299,648 kb)
  => the §6.8 lever assumption "~2,900 steps/segment at 48G" is REFUTED:
     2000 steps does NOT fit 48G.

-- fastseg-k1000 (36G cap, timeout 3600, fixed harness) --
tag=fastseg-k1000-36G rc=0 wall_s=239 peak_kb=29961284

decomposition over the three 350k points (k500: 148s/21.6GB from
records/fastseg.out; k1000: 239s/29.96GB; k2000: kill@~48G):
  marginal (500->1000): 0.182 s/step, 16.7 MB/step
  fixed: ~57 s, ~13.3 GB (import + ckpt literal + base)
  cross-check k2000: projected peak 13.25+2000*0.0167 = 46.7 GB ~ the 48G
  kill; projected wall 421 s vs 507 s observed (tail thrash near cap).

== emitter gate-check (24G cap; emitter-gatecheck.lean) ==
tag=emitter-gatecheck rc=0 wall_s=229 peak<=24G (cap-bounded; poll polluted)
  ONE incremental compiled pass emitting [350000, 350100]; kernel checks:
  (1) tk_350000 = ckptF350k  (batch-incremental == from-0 literal), and
  (2) the exact U5 segment shape, 100 steps equality-to-next-literal.
  Both PASS in 3:49 total => per-checkpoint emission ~15-30 s at 19k cells;
  the end-literal comparison adds ~10-20 s to a segment's fixed cost.

== re-projection at SEG=1000 (712 segments, last 616; GRP=16, 45 groups) ==
  kernel marginal 711,616 x 0.182 s               = 36.0 CPU-h  (band x0.18-0.25: 36-49)
  per-segment fixed 712 x ~57-70 s                = 11.3-13.8 CPU-h
  emission (712 literals ~20s + compiled passes)  = ~5.4 CPU-h
  composition + readout                           < 1 CPU-h
  CENTRAL ~53-55 CPU-h (band ~45-67)  vs the >60 CPU-h PAUSE trigger => GO
  memory: segment peak 13.3 + 1000*0.0167 = ~30 GB mid-run (+2-3 GB late-run
  literal growth) => 36G cap/segment; wave = lake -j2 in a 74G scope.
